Description: Fix C++23 incomplete type error for MediaLog in MojoVideoEncodeAccelerator
 C++23 libc++ requires complete types when instantiating unique_ptr's
 destructor. Using value initialization = {} instead of = nullptr avoids
 instantiating the destructor at the point of declaration while still
 providing null default behavior. This is the same fix pattern as patch
 0041 for gpu_video_encode_accelerator_factory.h.
Author: Juan Manuel Méndez Rey <vejeta@gmail.com>
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/915400
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2025-11-28

diff --git a/media/mojo/clients/mojo_video_encode_accelerator.h b/media/mojo/clients/mojo_video_encode_accelerator.h
index c438bf5..b7a9a0c 100644
--- a/media/mojo/clients/mojo_video_encode_accelerator.h
+++ b/media/mojo/clients/mojo_video_encode_accelerator.h
@@ -44,7 +44,7 @@ class MojoVideoEncodeAccelerator : public VideoEncodeAccelerator {
   EncoderStatus Initialize(
       const Config& config,
       Client* client,
-      std::unique_ptr<MediaLog> media_log = nullptr) override;
+      std::unique_ptr<MediaLog> media_log = {}) override;
   void Encode(scoped_refptr<VideoFrame> frame, bool force_keyframe) override;
   void Encode(scoped_refptr<VideoFrame> frame,
               const VideoEncoder::EncodeOptions&) override;
